Subject: [PATCH 1/7] relax: a program's own sources of a built-in macro
 package run on the JIT host

A program that pins another makepad revision as a git dependency (octos does,
for makepad-script) holds makepad_live_id and its macro crates with sources the
natively linked macros were not built from. Registration ended the run with
"crate substitution: the proc macros in this tree differ from those built into
relax ... source bytes differ".

Such a unit, and each built-in unit that reaches it, now leaves the native sets
at registration and its macros run on the JIT host, as any other proc macro's
do. A built-in unit apart from it stays native. An edit that makes a matching
package differ while the program runs is still reported by reload.

Graph::new validates every built-in name without reading the published graph.
The two unit tests take turns: SOURCE_READS is one counter for the process.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
